      "provenance": {
        "notes": "Zebra haworthia is easily mixed up with Haworthiopsis fasciata (smooth upper leaf surface); NC State says they are often mislabelled and cared for the same way. Watering: NC State lets the soil dry between waterings; the RHS genus guide waters only when the compost is nearly dry and almost not at all in winter; mapped to let_fully_dry (agent). A cool winter rest with only occasional light watering is needed (RHS genus guide), without numbers, so the rest factor is unknown. Temperature: RHS genus guide 10 to 26 C and always above 10 C; NC State 60 to 80 F, avoid below 50 F. Humidity: NC State says it tolerates normal home humidity, RHS wants low humidity: no figure. Size: NC State 4 to 12 in tall and 6 in to 2 ft wide, RHS about 12 cm rosette. Toxicity: NC State says non-toxic to pets and people; the ASPCA page read is for Haworthia fasciata (non-toxic to dogs and cats), so it is a related-species corroboration."
      },
